course: dictionary
lesson: 14482
title: Fatherly and family words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Paternal means of a father. Add -ly and you get paternally, which means in a fatherly way: kind, caring and protective, the way a father might look after you.
explain: Badger acts paternally towards Toad and Mole. He keeps them safe, gives them advice and tells them off when they need it. Ask yourself: is this how a caring father would act? If it is, paternally fits.
explain: The word has a second meaning about family. «My cousin is related to me paternally, through my dad's side.» Here paternally means on the father's side of the family. Try swapping in «on the father's side» to check, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Paternally means in a fatherly way: kind, caring or protective, like a father.
fact: «Paternally» can also mean on the father's side of a family.
fact: «Paternal» means of a father, and adding -ly makes it describe how someone acts or how someone is related.
fact: Badger acts paternally towards Toad and Mole in the stories, looking after them and giving them advice.
fact: A good check is to swap in «like a father» or «on the father's side» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The coach looked after the team paternally, making sure everyone was warm and fed.» What does the coach show? | *Kindness and care like a father | Boredom | Sadness | Anger and rudeness
exercise: «Badger spoke paternally to Toad, patting his shoulder and telling him to stop being so silly.» What does paternally mean here? | *In a fatherly, caring way | In an angry, shouting way | At top speed | In a sleepy, careless way
exercise: «My cousin is related to me paternally, through my dad's side of the family.» What does paternally mean here? | Very old and wise | *On the father's side of the family | At the family party | On the mother's side of the family
test: «The farmer checked on his young helpers paternally, asking if they were warm enough.» What does paternally suggest? | *Caring and protective, like a father | Bored and uninterested | Angry and loud | Fast and busy
test: «Lily's paternal aunt lives in Wales.» What does paternal mean here? | Kind and gentle | *On her father's side of the family | Very old | On her mother's side of the family
exam: «Mr Patel spoke paternally to the nervous boy, telling him it was all right to be scared.» What does paternally mean? | In a loud, excited way | *In a kind, caring, fatherly way | In a cross, bossy way | In a quick, careless way
